      "description": "Comprehensive test covering splash screen, version check, login, OTP verification, multiple mandatory popups, and the full credit limit increase request flow.",
      "workflow_narrative": "The user launches the app, bypasses a version check, and logs in with demo credentials. After entering a 6-digit OTP and dismissing legal, reminder, and notification popups, the user navigates from the dashboard to the 'Increase Limit' section. They select a specific card ending in 1234, request a new limit of 7500, accept the agreement, and confirm their submission. Finally, they verify the success message and return to the home dashboard.",
      "appium_implementation_guidance": [
        "Use WebDriverWait for the splash screen and version check button to handle app initialization time.",
        "OTP DETECTED: Read the code from the MOBILE_OTP environment variable at runtime and distribute digits across the 6 input fields.",
        "The dashboard loading state (~400ms) requires a short explicit wait before interacting with the menu button.",
        "Ensure the agreement checkbox is scrolled into view if necessary before tapping."
